2. Understand CRUD operations
CRUD represents four basic database operations.
Operation	Meaning	SQL	SQLAlchemy
Create	Insert a record	INSERT	db.add()
Read	Retrieve records	SELECT	db.query()
Update	Modify a record	UPDATE	Modify object + commit()
Delete	Remove a record	DELETE	db.delete()
In your AI platform, these operations will be used to manage AI request records.
For example:
•	Create: Save a new AI request.
•	Read: Retrieve a user's request history.
•	Update: Change a request's status.
•	Delete: Remove an unwanted request record.

3. Understand database relationships
Imagine your platform has 100 users.
Each user can submit multiple AI requests.
A typical database design looks like this:
Database relationship: One user → Many AI requests
users
id — Primary key
name
email

One-to-many
ai_requests
id — Primary key
request_id
user_id — Foreign key
model
prompt
total_tokens
One user can have multiple AI requests, but each request belongs to one user.
This is called a one-to-many relationship.
Today, we'll introduce a simple user table so you can implement this relationship in SQLAlchemy.
